  "description": "TANRUY crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C150 H112 Gd4 N12 O16 S6,5(C2 H3 N1),0.5(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.610-3.920 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.87-112.13°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C160.50H128ClGd4N17O16S6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
